+## Safety
+- Ask before anything hard to undo or outward-facing: pushing, posting comments, deleting, writing
+  to shared systems. Ask before every push.
+- Never put secrets, credentials or real personal names in code, commits, tests or docs. Use
+  placeholders like "User A".
 - Stop only processes you started, by their exact id, never by a name pattern.
 - Back up any config file before changing it for a test, and restore it afterwards.
+- Stop and ask when a step would delete user data, change a published number, or go against the
+  plan.
 
-### Commits and PRs
-- One meaningful changelog entry per change: what changed, who is affected, any migration.
-- Commit messages explain *why*, not just what.
-- Keep issue and PR text short and plain: before → after, and how it was tested.
