-## Project decisions (2026-10-02, override the generic rules above where they conflict)
-- Commit straight to `main`; no PR per change. Still: one change per commit, break-it review before asking to push, ask before every push.
-- Changelog lives in `CHANGELOG.md` (Keep a Changelog, `Unreleased` section); every commit that changes behaviour adds one entry.
-- Git hooks via the `pre-commit` framework (`.pre-commit-config.yaml`): pre-commit runs ruff check + ruff format check, pre-push runs the CI pytest command. Install in every clone with `uv run pre-commit install`.
-- Only English UI text exists, so the "every supported language" check is satisfied by English.
+## Commits
+- `Type(scope): Subject`, then `- ` bullets that explain *why*, not just what.
+- No AI co-author or "generated with" lines.
+- Keep issue text short and plain: before → after, and how it was tested.
